# Annaumixyz Equium

### CPU-mineable infrastructure on Solana

**Mine from any machine using the Equium protocol.**

[Docs](https://annaumixyz.xyz/docs) · [GitHub](https://github.com/annaumixyz/annaumixyz-equium) · [Follow on X](https://x.com/Annaumixyz)

</div>

---

## ✦ About

This repository contains the Equium mining infrastructure customized for the Annaumixyz ecosystem.

Equium is a CPU-oriented proof-of-work protocol designed to run efficiently on common hardware using Equihash. The project includes browser miners, desktop miners, and a CLI miner implementation built with Rust.

This repository is intended for educational purposes, self-hosted mining experiments, and infrastructure development on Solana.

---

## ✦ Features

- CPU-friendly mining algorithm
- Rust-based high performance miner
- Browser miner support
- Desktop application support
- CLI miner for VPS/server deployments
- Solana integration
- Multi-platform support (Linux, Windows, macOS)

---

## ✦ Requirements

Before running the project, install:

- Rust (latest stable)
- Cargo
- Git
- Solana CLI tools (optional)

---

## ✦ Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/annaumixyz/annaumixyz-equium.git
cd annaumixyz-equium
```

Build the project:

```bash
cargo build --release
```

---

## ✦ CLI Miner

Build the CLI miner:

```bash
cargo build -p annaumixyz-cli-miner --release
```

Run the miner:

```bash
./target/release/annaumixyz-miner \
  --rpc-url https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY \
  --keypair ~/.config/solana/id.json
```

---

## ✦ Configuration

Configuration files are located inside:

```bash
config/
```

You can customize:

- RPC endpoints
- Wallet/keypair paths
- Mining parameters
- Thread usage
- Network settings

---

## ✦ Wallet Setup

Generate a Solana wallet:

```bash
solana-keygen new
```

Your keypair file will be used by the miner for signing transactions.

---

## ✦ Recommended RPC

For stable mining performance, use a dedicated RPC provider such as:

- Helius
- QuickNode
- Alchemy

Public RPC endpoints may rate-limit requests during heavy mining activity.

---

## ✦ Project Structure

```bash
clients/        # Browser, desktop, and CLI miners
programs/       # Solana on-chain programs
config/         # Configuration files
scripts/        # Helper scripts
```

